 "notes": [
  "No printed number is a mismatch: every string the master prints on pages 14, 16 and 17 is the half-up rounding of the registry row given as its key. Axis labels 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 are coordinates and carry key null; ordinals (row 1, rows 2 and 3, step numbers, Result 1 and 2, page counters) and the citation years on page 16 are words, not numbers, and are not listed.",
  "The weak post-purchase cell uses p2_base_r0_low_profit_plus with Bprior_r0 in alt_keys. The chart label 'rho = 0.25' is prim_rho (build_results.js used entry_r0, same 1/4). The tick and text 1.97 is rJ: build_results.js (13 Nov) printed and shaded to rN = 1.75, and the master was changed to 1.97 since; that builder is stale on this point. All other contract keys are confirmed.",
  "The dashed grey stretch on pages 14 and 17 runs from rN = 1.75 (registry rN, printed nowhere) to rJ = 1.97. It is not the equilibrium with no informed order: it is the mixed-order equilibrium at the entry floor (form Q of handout/figures.js): class H buys and class L sells, each at rate s = t = b(rho Delta_T/k - 2) > 0, no order attracts the costly rival, entry is rho. The solid grey part from 1 to 1.75 is form N (no informed order), closed at 1.75. The master marks neither end at 1.75 and puts an open circle at 1.97 (Q excludes it). Page 14's bracket 'no informed order' covers only 1 to 1.39, so the master's words are not wrong, but page 17's 'If no informed order is expected, entry stays at rho ...' sits beside a branch that, from 1.75 to 1.97, has informed orders (page 17's note 'may mix over its best orders' covers it). No stop of the control falls in 1.75 to 1.97, so the control never lands on the dashed stretch.",
  "The ramp from 1.39 to rF = 1.47 (registry rF_B, printed nowhere) is form R, entry rho + (1 - rho) b Delta_T(r)/(2k): 0.45 at 1.39 (registry entry_rA_B) rising to 0.52 at 1.47. The master draws it as a straight solid segment (the manuscript and the handout draw R dashed). The curve lies below its chord by at most 0.00084 in entry, 0.55 px on the 1600 x 900 stage at the master's scale: the sampled curve and the master's chord are the same picture.",
  "The claim on page 14 says 'entry is about 0.52 from 1.39 to 3.59'; the closed form gives 0.45 at 1.39 and reaches 0.52 only at 1.47. A control stop at 1.39 that prints entry at each dot would show 0.45 (entry_rA_B, printed nowhere in the master) beside that claim. Decide whether the control prints entry at 1.39 or shows the dot only.",
  "Control numbers with no registry row at that strength: entry 0.25 at 1.39 (prim_rho; the branch with no informed order has entry rho at every strength, but no row states it at rA), and entry 0.52 at 1.97 and at 3.59 (entry_r1_B, a row stated at r1; the closed form rho + (1 - rho)(b + lambda/2) is the same on the whole flat stretch from rF to rC, and p4_frozen_entry_below_ceiling states it for 1 < r <= rC, but with orders held fixed). They are right by the closed form; they are not certain registry rows. The other control numbers are rows at their own strength (entry_r0, entry_rA_B, entry_r2, prim_r0, rA, rJ, prim_r1, rC_B, prim_r2).",
  "Page 14's middle bracket ('a purchase raises the belief and attracts the costly rival', shape 41 over path 36) starts at rF = 1.47, not at 1.39: the ramp from 1.39 to 1.47 sits under no bracket, although a purchase attracts the costly rival there too (form R recruits after a purchase). curves.pages.p14.brackets keeps the master's span.",
  "Endpoints from the closed forms (handout/figures.js equilibria, tie rule of page 17's note): no informed order for r <= rN (1.75); the ramp for rA <= r < rF (closed at 1.39, filled circle in the master); the flat stretch for rF <= r <= rC (closed at 3.59, filled circle); the stretch at rho for r > rC (open at 3.59; the manuscript draws an open circle there, the master draws none); the dashed stretch for rN < r < rJ (open at both ends). Two equilibria at every r in [1.39, 1.97): no informed order with the ramp on [1.39, 1.47), with the flat stretch on [1.47, 1.75], the dashed stretch with the flat stretch on (1.75, 1.97). At 1.97 itself only the flat stretch: the shading's right edge is excluded, as the master's open circle shows.",
  "The vertical drop at 3.59 (pages 14, 16, 17) is a connector, not an equilibrium: no strength has an entry between rho and 0.52 there. The master draws it 1.25 pt and dotted; it carries no data, so the 3 px floor for data lines does not bind it. data.json marks it connector: true.",
  "Page 16, 'orders held fixed': full orders at every strength (form F with s = lambda); entry is p4_frozen_entry_below_ceiling (= entry_r1_B, 0.52) for 1 < r <= rC and p4_frozen_entry_above_ceiling (rho) after. Its stretch after 3.59 is dashed only in the older render (whose colour, orange, the dump contradicts: #1B3A6B); the dump records no dash pattern, so that style is unconfirmed. Three lines lie on rho from 3.59 to 4.5: it, 'price hidden from the rival' and the pale full-model trace; a dash lets all three show there.",
  "Page 16, 'price hidden from the rival': entry rho at every strength, because the rival prepares on the prior and B_r(1/2) <= B_1(1/2) = 4.875 < c_H = 6 on the whole axis (B falls in r). Registry rows exist only at the incumbents (p4_hidden_r0_entry, p4_hidden_r1_entry, p2_base_hidden_entry: 0.25); beyond r1 the line is the closed form alone.",
  "Page 16's pale 'full model' trace in the dump is: no informed order from 1 to rN (shape 5), the ramp and the flat stretch (shape 6), and the stretch at rho after 3.59 (shape 7). It leaves out the dashed stretch, the drop and the endpoint circles; curves.pages.p16.trace lists those segments.",
  "Under the other tie rule (an indifferent costly rival may prepare with any probability), the threshold pair T adds an equilibrium on [1.39, 1.97] (handout/explorer.js draws it thin and dashed). The master and this data leave it out.",
  "The control stops 3.59 (rC) and 3.6 (r2) are 1.49 px apart on the stage at the master's scale; the marker, the dots and the two labels at these stops must not rely on their x position alone to be told apart.",
  "Placement noise in the master, all under 1.5 pt on its 960 x 540 page (read from its boxes on page 14): the flat stretch at 0.5191 against 0.5228, the ramp start at 0.4515 against 0.4542, rA at 1.391, rF at 1.469, rN at 1.749, rJ at 1.972, rC at 3.590, r2 at 3.602. data.json gives the closed-form positions; the '0.52' tick sits at the closed-form 0.5228.",
  "Closed forms against their registry rows (build log): the largest difference over 12 checks is 2.31E-16 (B_rC(M) - c_H at the rounded registry rC_B is rounding noise; which side of 3.59 a branch takes is decided by comparing registry rows, never by that sign)."
 ]
